---
name: angular-conventions
description: Coding conventions for {{ project_name }} - Angular standalone components, npm, ESLint/Prettier, Karma specs.
---

This is an Angular single-page app managed with `npm`. Follow these conventions for every
change:

- Manage dependencies with `npm install` / `npm install --save-dev`; never hand-edit the
  version ranges in `package.json`, and never call `pip` — this is a Node project.
- Run everything through the `package.json` scripts or `npx`: `npm start` (`ng serve`),
  `npm run build`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npx ng generate ...`.
- Components, directives and pipes are **standalone**. Do not introduce `NgModule`s. Use
  `npx ng generate component features/<name>` so new pieces match the workspace layout.
- String literals use single quotes, enforced by Prettier (`.prettierrc.json`) and
  `npm run lint`.
- Prefer signals and the modern control-flow syntax (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`) in
  templates over the older structural directives.
- Every new component or service under `src/app/` needs a matching `*.spec.ts`. The
  pre-commit hook runs `npm run lint` and the full Karma/Jasmine suite (headless Chromium)
  and both must pass.
